# {{ .Env }} mksrv workspace

This directory is a **private mksrv workspace**. It holds real deployment data:
hostnames, account identifiers, and DNS zones. Secrets never live in this
directory — they resolve from AWS SSM Parameter Store at runtime. Keep this
workspace in a **separate private repository** — never inside the public
`mksrv` engine repository.

## Layout

```
deployment.yaml      environment, AWS, backend, DNS, identity, and fleet hosts
tenants/<id>.yaml    one client company; all service FQDNs derive from base_domain
tenants/<id>.users.yaml   optional declarative user list
mksrv.lock           engine version of the last successful apply
.mksrv/              generated Terraform inputs, plans, outputs, and local state
```

## Next steps

1. Edit `deployment.yaml`: set the Route 53 `zone_id`, confirm the region and
   host layout, and adjust `mgmt_cidr` to your operator network.
2. Add tenant documents under `tenants/`.
3. Validate: `mksrv validate` and `mksrv doctor`.
4. Provision infrastructure: `mksrv plan --infra-only` then
   `mksrv apply --infra-only`.
